{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>את ה׳ האמרת היום.</b> This is an expression of elevation and height, from the root of (Isaiah 17:6) בראש אמיר, which is the highest branch. And so Onkelos translated it חטבת, from the root of (Proverbs 7:16) חטובות אטון מצרים, ' choice ones.' And they said in the name of R. Yehudah HaLevi, of blessed memory, that it is from the root of ויאמר, that is to say: you did what is right in His eyes by accepting His Torah, to the point that you brought it about that He said that He would be ה׳ אלהיך."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Isaiah citation given as ישעיהו י״ז:ו׳ (17:6); the phrase בראש אמיר indeed appears in Isaiah 17:6 — citation normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:20.468648394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}